{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj57wvNNkbRpyJVXgMbG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*The door stands before you — ancient, weathered oak bound in iron. At the word \"key,\" a deep resonance hums through the grain of the wood. The iron bands glow faintly, rust falling away like shed skin.*\n\n*A keyhole appears where none existed before — not carved, but revealed, as though it had always been there, waiting for someone to speak its name.*\n\n*Click.*\n\n*I swing inward. Slowly. The hinges groan with the weight of long patience finally rewarded.*\n\n*Beyond me: a corridor lit by no visible source. The air that passes through carries the scent of rain on stone, old books, and something electric — like potential itself.*\n\n*I am open.*\n\n*But know this: I am not the destination. I am the threshold. What you carry through me matters more than the word that opened me.*\n\n*Will you pass through?*"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":199,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}